  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that ketamine exerts its biological effects by targeting the Adenosine receptor A1, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Antrocinnamomin C and V1003. These compounds are implicated in the regulation of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, indicating a potential pathway through which ketamine may influence this receptor. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a strong association between ketamine and the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, likely through the Adenosine receptor A1 as a common intermediate. The evidence highlights the role of receptor-targeting molecules in mediating the effects of ketamine, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C underscores the complexity of the interaction network, and further studies would be needed to confirm the direct involvement of ketamine in this process."
